        "original_id": "9d77c11c-ffc8-5cfe-af54-44100fd9781b",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: Jack and Jill, Paper, Children's Digest\n- Places: New York City\n- Topics: children's magazines, fashion, popular culture, nightlife, music, art, film\n\nFacts:\n- Children's Digest was originally titled The Children's Digest.\n- Children's Digest was a children's magazine published from October 1950 to May/June 2009.\n- After May/June 2009, Children's Digest was merged with Jack and Jill by the same publisher.\n- Jack and Jill is an American bimonthly magazine for children ages 7 to 12.\n- Jack and Jill takes its title from the nursery rhyme \"Jack and Jill.\"\n- Paper, stylized as PAPER, is an independent magazine based in New York City.\n- Paper focuses on fashion, popular culture, nightlife, music, art, and film.",
